# Continuation refusal lint in lazy quotes

## Root cause

The classifier identifies a lone `+` at an unmatched column in an open list and quote, but the lint collector skips that decision when the quote continues lazily without a parsed first block. The marker remains text, while its refusal goes unreported.

## Spec ruling

PART 9 §17 L3 says: “The `continuation-marker-refused` lint reports every refusal.” The two no-warning expectations for `between list and quote` and `past quote column` conflict with this clause.

## Change

Record a wrong-column refusal when the classifier finds no owner and an open container still exists on a quoted line or after an indented quote. Use the classifier's decision, including its source position, rather than the two listed inputs' numeric columns. Change only the two stale expectations.

## Scope

The rule covers standalone markers at columns no open container owns during those lazy quote paths. It does not depend on the particular list text or the marker's numeric column.
